=================================================================
What is TCP?
=================================================================
TCP (Transmission Control Protocol) is a Layer 4 (Transport layer) protocol that provides reliable, ordered, and error-checked delivery of data between two hosts.


=================================================================
Key Features of TCP (memorize these)
=================================================================
Connection-oriented

Reliable delivery

Ordered packets

Error detection & retransmission

Flow control

Congestion control

=================================================================
TCP 3-Way Handshake 
=================================================================
Purpose

To establish a reliable connection before data transfer.

Steps

SYN – Client → Server (request to connect)

SYN-ACK – Server → Client (acknowledge + agree)

ACK – Client → Server (connection established)

📌 After this, data transfer begins.


=================================================================
TCP Connection Termination (4-Way Handshake)
=================================================================
FIN → request close

ACK → acknowledge

FIN → close from other side

ACK → connection closed
=================================================================
TCP vs UDP (classic comparison)
=================================================================
TCP	UDP
Reliable	Unreliable
Connection-oriented	Connectionless
Slower	Faster
Ordered packets	No order guarantee
Retransmission	No retransmission
Used by HTTP, HTTPS, SSH	Used by DNS, VoIP, streaming

